# Copy this file to `deploy.env` and fill in real values.
#
# deploy.ps1 uploads `deploy.env` to the VM and merges each KEY=value line
# ADDITIVELY into <VmPath>/server.env: only the keys listed here are added or
# updated, everything else already on the VM (DATABASE_URL, ...) stays.
# The first deploy creates the Postgres database and its DATABASE_URL on the
# VM, so you don't need to set it here.
#
# `deploy.env` is gitignored. Never commit real secrets.

# Google sign-in: Google Cloud Console > APIs & Services > Credentials >
# OAuth client ID (Web application). Authorized redirect URI:
#   <PUBLIC_URL>/v1/auth/google/callback
GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=

# Discord sign-in: Discord Developer Portal > your app > OAuth2. Redirect:
#   <PUBLIC_URL>/v1/auth/discord/callback
DISCORD_CLIENT_ID=
DISCORD_CLIENT_SECRET=

# Set automatically from -Domain (https://<domain>) or the VM address
# (http://<VmHost>:8080). Only set it to override that.
# PUBLIC_URL=

# Name-only test login. Leave off on a public server.
# DEV_LOGIN=false

# Admin page (<PUBLIC_URL>/admin) for events, gifts, seasons and rewards.
# Leave empty to keep it switched off. Make a long random key, at least 20
# characters. In PowerShell:
#   -join ((48..57)+(65..90)+(97..122) | Get-Random -Count 32 | % {[char]$_})
# Only use the admin page over https (deploy with -Domain), otherwise the
# key travels unencrypted.
# ADMIN_KEY=

# Sizing. deploy.ps1 picks these from the VM itself on every deploy (see
# README "How many players"): a 1 GB Azure VM gets MAX_ONLINE_BRAIN=256,
# DB_POOL=6; a 24 GB Oracle Ampere box gets 1024 and 12; KEEP_RAIDS_DAYS
# follows the disk. Only uncomment one to force it; a line here always wins
# over the automatic choice, so don't copy small-VM values to a big machine.
#
# Biggest brain taken online. Allowed: 64, 128, 256, 512, 1024.
# MAX_ONLINE_BRAIN=256
# Days finished raids stay in the battle log (each keeps both armies for the
# replay: about 4 MB with 256 brains, 33 MB with 1024).
# KEEP_RAIDS_DAYS=3
# Database connections (each keeps buffers as big as the biggest base or army
# it has moved, so fewer means less memory).
# DB_POOL=6
